.TH "lectos" "1" "2026\-10\-13" "lectos 0.1.0" "General Commands Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
lectos \- presenter console and projector for PDF slides with Markdown or Beamer notes
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBlectos\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPDF\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR] [\fINOTES\fR]
.br
\fBlectos\-tui\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPDF\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR [\fINOTES\fR]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBlectos\fR shows your slides (a compiled PDF) to the audience in a projector window and gives you a presenter
console: the current, projected and next slide, your notes, a timer with your standing against the plan, an overview
grid, search, freeze and blackout for the projector, a chalkboard, ink, and a laser pointer.\&
.PP
Without arguments \fBlectos\fR opens a window to choose the slides, the notes and folders.\& Given only the PDF it uses the
notes next to it (\fIslides.\&tex\fR, \fIslides.\&md\fR, else \fInotes.\&tex\fR, \fInotes.\&md\fR); given a folder it uses the PDF in it.\&
.PP
\fINOTES\fR is a Markdown file (sections tied to slides with \fB<!\&\-\- slide: N \-\->\fR markers, LaTeX math between \fB$\fR signs) or
a Beamer \fB.\&tex\fR file, whose \fB\enote{}\fR commands become the notes.\& \fBlectos\fR never compiles anything: build the PDF
yourself.\&
.PP
The console and the projector are chosen independently.\& The console is \fBgtk\fR (libadwaita) or \fBtui\fR (terminal); the
projector is \fBgtk\fR (a window of its own, which supports blackout, chalkboard, ink and laser), \fBzathura\fR (a Zathura window
driven over D\-Bus) or \fBnone\fR.\& \fBlectos\-tui\fR starts the terminal console with Zathura and needs no GTK.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-\-console\fR \fIgtk\fR|\fItui\fR
.RS 4
Presenter interface.\& Default: \fBgtk\fR, or \fBconsole\fR under \fB[ui]\fR in the options file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-projector\fR \fIgtk\fR|\fIzathura\fR|\fInone\fR
.RS 4
Audience window.\& Default: \fBgtk\fR (\fBzathura\fR for \fBlectos\-tui\fR), or \fBprojector\fR under \fB[ui]\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-layout\fR \fIauto\fR|\fIcompact\fR|\fIwide\fR|\fIdraw\fR
.RS 4
GTK console layout: for a notebook, for a big screen (adds a filmstrip of previous and upcoming slides), chosen by
window width, or the quick drawing layout (large slide, drawing toolbar).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fIauto\fR|\fIen\fR|\fIru\fR|\fIde\fR
.RS 4
Interface language.\& Default: from \fBLC_ALL\fR, \fBLANGUAGE\fR, \fBLANG\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-windowed\fR
.RS 4
Keep the GTK projector window windowed.\& It is fullscreen on the last monitor when there are several.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-monitor\fR \fIN\fR
.RS 4
Monitor index for the GTK projector window.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-fullscreen\fR
.RS 4
Start the projector fullscreen.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-vim\fR
.RS 4
Start with vim keys off (GTK console).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Options file.\& Default: \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lectos/options.\&toml\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-version\fR, \fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Print the version or the usage.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH KEYS
.PP
Arrows, Space, Page Up/Down, Home and End always navigate.\& Vim keys are on by default in the GTK console and always on
in the terminal console:
.PP
\fBl\fR, \fBh\fR
.RS 4
next, previous slide (a count works: \fB5l\fR)
.PP
.RE
\fBgg\fR, \fBG\fR, \fB12G\fR, \fB:12\fR
.RS 4
first, last, slide 12
.PP
.RE
\fBj\fR, \fBk\fR
.RS 4
scroll the notes
.PP
.RE
\fB:\fR
.RS 4
command line; Tab completes.\& \fB:help\fR lists every command, \fB?\&\fR opens the same list.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB/\fR, \fBn\fR, \fBN\fR
.RS 4
search slides and notes, next and previous hit
.PP
.RE
\fBo\fR, \fBz\fR, \fBb\fR, \fBB\fR, \fBp\fR, \fBt\fR
.RS 4
overview, freeze, blackout, chalkboard, laser pointer, timer
.PP
.RE
\fBf\fR, \fBF\fR
.RS 4
projector fullscreen, console fullscreen
.PP
.RE
\fBs\fR, \fBE\fR, \fBS\fR
.RS 4
quick drawing layout, edit this slide'\&s notes, settings window
.PP
.RE
Every button and menu entry is also a command, for example \fB:target 1h30\fR, \fB:color red\fR, \fB:clear\-all\fR, \fB:export\fR, \fB:panel strip off\fR, \fB:export\-ink\fR.\&
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lectos/options.\&toml\fR
.RS 4
Options: blackout screen, console and header contents, drawing and laser defaults, language.\& See the example in the
source tree.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/lectos/\fR
.RS 4
Per\-presentation recovery state (current slide, timer, layout, hidden panels) and ink, as small JSON files, and
notes you edited for a Beamer deck (the \fI.\&tex\fR itself is never changed).\&
.PP
.RE
\fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/lectos/math/\fR
.RS 4
Cached formula images.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBLC_ALL\fR, \fBLC_MESSAGES\fR, \fBLANGUAGE\fR, \fBLANG\fR
.RS 4
Select the interface language.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
.RS 4
Where the files above live (defaults under \fB\(ti/.\&config\fR, \fB\(ti/.\&local/state\fR, \fB\(ti/.\&cache\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Present with Beamer notes, GTK console and projector:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
lectos slides\&.pdf slides\&.tex
.fi
.RE
.PP
Terminal console with a Zathura projector, Markdown notes:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
lectos\-tui slides\&.pdf notes\&.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
0 on a normal exit, 1 when a viewer, a poppler tool or LaTeX fails, 2 for bad arguments or options.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBzathura\fR(1), \fBpdftoppm\fR(1), \fBpdftotext\fR(1), \fBchafa\fR(1), \fBlatex\fR(1), \fBdvipng\fR(1)
.PP
